                            <td class="p-3 border-b">Medium</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="p-3 border-b">Zakat</td>
                            <td class="p-3 border-b">Everyone who pays Zakat</td
                            >
                            <td class="p-3 border-b">Very Low</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="p-3 border-b">Shares</td>
                            <td class="p-3 border-b">Long-term investors</td>
                            <td class="p-3 border-b">Medium</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="p-3 border-b">House Loan</td>
                            <td class="p-3 border-b"
                                >Homeowners with active loans</td
                            >
                            <td class="p-3 border-b">Medium</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="p-3">Medical Allowance</td>
                            <td class="p-3">All salaried employees</td>
                            <td class="p-3">Very Low</td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-3">Practical Advice</h2>
            <p>
                Here are the key takeaways from years of tax filing best
                practices:
            </p>
            <p>
                <strong>Start with Zakat and VPS.</strong> These are the two easiest
                and most impactful options. Zakat is something most Pakistanis already
                pay — just make sure you're claiming it. VPS is something you should
                be doing anyway for retirement, and the tax credit makes it even more
                valuable.
            </p>
            <p>
                <strong>Keep documentation.</strong> For every tax credit you claim,
                keep the receipts, statements, and certificates. FBR can ask for proof
                at any time.
            </p>
            <p>
                <strong>Talk to your HR.</strong> Many employers will adjust your
                monthly tax deductions if you provide them with proof of your tax-saving
                investments. This means you benefit immediately rather than waiting
                for a refund.
            </p>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-3">
                Frequently Asked Questions
            </h2>
            <div class="space-y-4 mt-3">
                <div>
                    <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900">
                        Can I claim multiple tax credits in one year?
                    </h3>
                    <p class="text-gray-700 mt-1">
                        Yes, you can claim multiple tax credits. For example,
                        you can claim a VPS credit and a donation credit in the
                        same year. However, for investment in shares and life
                        insurance, you must choose one — not both.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900">
                        What is the deadline for making tax-saving investments?
                    </h3>
                    <p class="text-gray-700 mt-1">
                        The tax year in Pakistan runs from July 1 to June 30.
                        All investments must be made within the tax year to
                        qualify for that year's credit.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900">
                        Can I carry forward unused tax credits?
                    </h3>
                    <p class="text-gray-700 mt-1">
                        No. Any tax credit that cannot be utilized in a given
                        year cannot be refunded, carried forward, or carried
                        back.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900">
                        Are these tax savings legal?
                    </h3>
                    <p class="text-gray-700 mt-1">
                        Yes, absolutely. These are all provisions specifically
                        written into the Income Tax Ordinance 2001 by the
                        government to encourage saving, investment, and
                        charitable giving.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900">
                        What happens if I withdraw from VPS early?
                    </h3>
                    <p class="text-gray-700 mt-1">
                        Early withdrawal from VPS triggers a tax penalty equal
                        to your average tax rate over the preceding three years
                        . VPS is designed for retirement, not short-term gains.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-3">Final Thoughts</h2>
            <p>
                The Pakistani tax system isn't just about paying — it's also
                about planning. Every rupee you legally save on tax is a rupee
                you can invest, save, or spend on your family.
            </p>
            <p>
                Start with Zakat and VPS. Keep your documentation. Talk to your
                HR. And use our{" "}
                <a
                    href="/tools/salary-tax-calculator/"
                    class="text-blue-600 hover:underline font-medium"
                >
                    free Salary Tax Calculator
                </a>{" "}
                to see exactly how much tax you're paying — and how much you could
                save.
            </p>
        </section>

